## 7. Memory Layout Constraints

```
ESP32 Memory Map (relevant regions):
0x3FFAE000 – 0x3FFAFFFF : 4KB DMA-safe IRAM (DMA_BUFFER_A)
0x3FFB0000 – 0x3FFBFFFF : 64KB DRAM (heap, data, bss)
0x3FF40000 – 0x3FF7FFFF : 256KB DRAM (app CPU cache range)

Alignment requirements:
  • DMA buffers must be 4-byte aligned (word boundary)
  • FFT buffers for dsps_fft4r require 16-byte alignment (Xtensa SIMD VREG width)
  • ISR handler must be in IRAM (ESP_INTR_FLAG_IRAM) → code in .iram.text
  • All buffers declared DRAM_ATTR → stored in SRAM, not flash-mapped

Cache coherency:
  • DMA writes directly to SRAM (no cache involvement for IRAM region)
  • No cache flush/invalidate needed for IRAM buffers
  • Flash-mapped buffers (via spi_flash_read) require xthal_get_ccount sync
```

