## 1. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW

The ESP32 contains two I2S controllers (I2S0, I2S1) each with dedicated DMA channels. This document covers the **double-buffer ring architecture** used for continuous audio streaming without CPU intervention.

### 1.1 Memory Map - DMA Descriptors

```c
// ESP32 DMA Descriptor Structure (32-byte aligned)
typedef struct {
    uint32_t buffer;      // Physical RAM address (must be word-aligned)
    uint16_t dma_len;     // Transfer length in bytes (max 4095)
    uint16_t length;      // Same as dma_len for ESP32
    uint8_t  offset;      // Reserved (0x00)
    uint8_t  owner;       // 0x01 = CPU owns, 0x02 = DMA owns
    uint8_t  eof;         // End-of-frame flag (1 = triggers interrupt)
    uint8_t  sub_sof;     // Reserved (0x00)
} dma_desc_t;

// Static_assert: sizeof(dma_desc_t) == 12 bytes
_Static_assert(sizeof(dma_desc_t) == 12, "DMA descriptor size mismatch");
```

